From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Stockdale <jstockdale@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:23:28 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Input: nt36536: report the pen through touchscreen_report_pos
 like the finger

Ours (2026-11-02, A.3 stylus). Exit: submit to Perpetua together with the pen
capabilities patch.

The finger goes through touchscreen_report_pos() with the properties parsed
from the device tree (touchscreen-size-x/-y, -inverted-x, -swapped-x-y), so
it comes out in the panel's landscape frame. The pen's ABS_X/ABS_Y were
reported raw, in the controller's portrait frame, on axes sized from the
header defaults TOUCH_DEFAULT_MAX_WIDTH/HEIGHT (33920 x 24000, the landscape
pair): a raw Y of up to 33919 on an axis declared 0..23999, nothing inverted
or swapped, so the pen agreed with the finger nowhere but at the origin.

The pen shares the finger's coordinate frame: the stock device tree gives
both the same range (touchpanel,panel-coords = touchpanel,pen-panel-coords =
<0x5dc0 0x8480>, 24000 x 33920), and the packet's 16-bit X/Y need no scaling.
Size the pen's ABS_X/ABS_Y from the finger's parsed ABS_MT_POSITION_X/Y
(minimum, maximum and fuzz after the swap), which touchscreen_parse_properties()
already holds in the landscape frame, and report the pen's position with
touchscreen_report_pos(..., false) through the same properties; a raw
coordinate beyond the controller's range is clamped first so the inversion
cannot wrap. The resolution the previous patch sets on the pen's axes is
computed from these ranges and comes after them, so it follows along. The
release paths keep parking the pen at 0/0, which is inside the range on both
axes.

INPUT_PROP_DIRECT stays set on the pen device: systemd's input_id tags the
device ID_INPUT_TABLET from BTN_TOOL_PEN/BTN_STYLUS whatever the property, and
libinput (1.31) accepts a tablet once it has ABS_X/ABS_Y, BTN_TOOL_PEN or
BTN_STYLUS and a resolution on both axes (tablet_reject_device), then uses
INPUT_PROP_DIRECT to treat it as a display-integrated tablet: the calibration
matrix is offered (tablet_init_calibration) and the area configuration of
external tablets is not (tablet_init_area).

Signed-off-by: John Stockdale <jstockdale@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c
index 5df045d6d6db..85601b857c86 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c
@@ -1017,8 +1017,11 @@ static irqreturn_t nvt_ts_work_func(int irq, void *data)
 //				printk("x=%d,y=%d,p=%d,tx=%d,ty=%d,d=%d,b1=%d,b2=%d,bat=%d\n", pen_x, pen_y, pen_pressure,
 //						pen_tilt_x, pen_tilt_y, pen_distance, pen_btn1, pen_btn2, pen_battery);
 
-				input_report_abs(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_X, pen_x);
-				input_report_abs(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_Y, pen_y);
+				/* the finger's frame; clamp so the inversion cannot wrap */
+				pen_x = min_t(uint32_t, pen_x, ts->prop.max_x);
+				pen_y = min_t(uint32_t, pen_y, ts->prop.max_y);
+				touchscreen_report_pos(ts->pen_input_dev, &ts->prop,
+						       pen_x, pen_y, false);
 				input_report_abs(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_PRESSURE, pen_pressure);
 				input_report_key(ts->pen_input_dev, BTN_TOUCH, !!pen_pressure);
 				input_report_abs(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_TILT_X, pen_tilt_x);
@@ -1415,8 +1418,20 @@ static int32_t nvt_ts_probe(struct spi_device *client)
 		//ts->pen_input_dev->keybit[BIT_WORD(BTN_TOOL_RUBBER)] |= BIT_MASK(BTN_TOOL_RUBBER);
 		ts->pen_input_dev->propbit[0] = BIT(INPUT_PROP_DIRECT);
 
-		input_set_abs_params(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_X, 0, ts->abs_x_max - 1, 0, 0);
-		input_set_abs_params(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_Y, 0, ts->abs_y_max - 1, 0, 0);
+		/*
+		 * The pen reports in the finger's controller frame (the stock
+		 * device tree gives both 24000 x 33920 units): its axes take the
+		 * finger's parsed ranges and its position goes through the same
+		 * touchscreen_report_pos() transform.
+		 */
+		input_set_abs_params(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_X,
+				     input_abs_get_min(ts->input_dev, ABS_MT_POSITION_X),
+				     input_abs_get_max(ts->input_dev, ABS_MT_POSITION_X),
+				     input_abs_get_fuzz(ts->input_dev, ABS_MT_POSITION_X), 0);
+		input_set_abs_params(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_Y,
+				     input_abs_get_min(ts->input_dev, ABS_MT_POSITION_Y),
+				     input_abs_get_max(ts->input_dev, ABS_MT_POSITION_Y),
+				     input_abs_get_fuzz(ts->input_dev, ABS_MT_POSITION_Y), 0);
 		input_set_abs_params(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_PRESSURE, 0, PEN_PRESSURE_MAX, 0, 0);
 		input_set_abs_params(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_DISTANCE, 0, PEN_DISTANCE_MAX, 0, 0);
 		input_set_abs_params(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_TILT_X, PEN_TILT_MIN, PEN_TILT_MAX, 0, 0);
-- 
